# Copy to .env.local for local development. Every value is read at boot.

# Where the SQLite file and uploaded documents live. Relative to the repo root.
DB_PATH=./data/strategy.sqlite

# The two users. Seeded ONLY when the users table is empty; changing these
# later does nothing (use the change-password page instead).
USER1_EMAIL=alex@example.com
USER1_PASSWORD=change-me-please
USER1_NAME=Alex
USER2_EMAIL=jamie@example.com
USER2_PASSWORD=change-me-too
USER2_NAME=Jamie

# Amazon Bedrock: where every call that carries customer data goes.
# Credentials come from the AWS credential chain (instance role in prod,
# `AWS_PROFILE` or ~/.aws/credentials locally). No keys in this file.
#
# Use the US inference profile with Bedrock Runtime Invoke (not Mantle):
# structured calls require output_config.format. Confirm profile access in
# your region first; `npm run smoke:providers` proves the choice answers.
# This profile routes within the US, not globally.
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5

# What a model actually charges, per million tokens in US dollars.
#
# AWS bills Bedrock at its own rates and does not publish them anywhere this
# app can read, so nothing is assumed: until you set these, a run's cost is
# derived from published list prices and is labelled "estimated" everywhere it
# appears. Set them and the label goes away.
#
# The variable name is the model id uppercased with every non-alphanumeric
# character replaced by an underscore. For `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`:
#   AI_PRICE_US_ANTHROPIC_CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5_INPUT=
#   AI_PRICE_US_ANTHROPIC_CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5_OUTPUT=
#   AI_PRICE_US_ANTHROPIC_CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5_CACHE_READ=
#   AI_PRICE_US_ANTHROPIC_CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5_CACHE_WRITE=
# Cache rates are optional; omitted values retain the model's baseline cache
# rates (they are not recomputed from an overridden input rate). Opus 5.5 uses
# a 5% cache-read multiplier. The US Bedrock fallback includes the 10% regional
# premium and remains labelled estimated until deployed rates are supplied.
#
# The research model is priced under its own name, derived the same way from
# DIRECT_MODEL_ID — `claude-opus-5-5` gives AI_PRICE_CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5_INPUT and so
# on. It is easy to miss because the direct API publishes its list prices, so
# that cost is not labelled an estimate and looks settled; setting a real rate
# is still what makes it true. Web search and fetch are billed per request
# rather than per token, and default to their published rates — see
# AI_PRICE_WEB_SEARCH_PER_1K_USD below.
#
# Every one of these names changes when the model id does, and a rate left
# under the old name is inert rather than wrong — no error, and a cost line
# that goes on calling itself an estimate. tests/priceOverrides.test.ts
# derives the expected names from the configured ids so that cannot pass
# quietly.

# Direct Anthropic API: used ONLY for web research, which sends the account's
# name, headquarters and region and the question you type. Nothing from the
# deals, people, meetings or install base can reach it.
DIRECT_MODEL_ID=claude-opus-5-5
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Web search and page fetch are billed per request, and no token count shows
# it. Both default to the rates Anthropic publishes — $10 per 1,000 searches,
# and nothing at all for a fetch, which pays only for the tokens it returns —
# so a deployment that sets neither already counts them. Set one only to say
# something different, in US dollars per thousand requests.
#   AI_PRICE_WEB_SEARCH_PER_1K_USD=
#   AI_PRICE_WEB_FETCH_PER_1K_USD=

# Refuse new AI runs once today's spend reaches this many cents. "Today" is
# the timezone below, so the cap rolls over at your midnight.
AI_DAILY_CAP_CENTS=1500

# The timezone the app lives in. It decides what "today" means everywhere:
# which meetings are coming up, what is overdue, the date stamped on an
# import, and when the fiscal quarter turns over. Any IANA name; an
# unrecognised one falls back to the default with a warning in the log.
APP_TIMEZONE=America/Los_Angeles

# Month (1-12) in which the fiscal year starts. FY is named for the calendar
# year in which it ends. The value derived from this is only a default; the
# fiscal quarter stored on each deal can be edited.
FISCAL_YEAR_START_MONTH=8

# Set to 1 to replace every model call with canned data (local demo / tests).
AI_FAKE=0
